Yes we need to define the responder info for each device type eg:
struct ResponderInfo
{
    sdbusplus::message::object_path path;
    std::variant<MctpResponderInfo, TcpResponderInfo> info;
    TransportType transport;
};

There could be two scenario:
   Mapper is down / call failed -> returns {}
   Mapper succeeded but no endpoints exist -> also returns {}


In both cases, discovery has nothing to act on and doesn't need to distinguish between them. If the mapper call fails, the error is already logged with full context (interface name, error details) at the by_interface catch.

